1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,010
What if the places we pass every day became worlds we could play in?

2
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:07,670
Meet Blockplay S G.

3
00:00:07,670 --> 00:00:08,500
Singapore, playable.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:15,895
Walk, drive, and discover familiar places across Marina Bay, Queenstown, and Raffles Place.

5
00:00:15,895 --> 00:00:19,500
Collect stamps as you explore each neighbourhood.

6
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,796
Want somewhere closer?

7
00:00:21,796 --> 00:00:27,116
Ask your companion, and your destination updates on the map.

8
00:00:27,116 --> 00:00:33,500
Luna interprets the request, while the game checks and applies the change.

9
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:38,492
In Queenstown, everyday spaces become places to explore and learn.

10
00:00:38,492 --> 00:00:44,500
Ask about a nearby stop, and discover local stories with links to their sources.

11
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:49,061
Our worlds start with Google Maps Street View references.

12
00:00:49,061 --> 00:00:56,782
Here, Astra helped refine Raffles Place using new images: two window bands, green trim, and a sloping awning.

13
00:00:56,782 --> 00:01:01,500
Each reviewed iteration can bring more detail into the playable world.

14
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:11,051
As a team of two, we used Astra to coordinate region agents, build the worlds, fix gameplay issues, and check the results.

15
00:01:11,051 --> 00:01:15,477
Agents worked in parallel, with shared browser checks coordinated in sequence.

16
00:01:15,477 --> 00:01:19,500
The optional voice companion uses G P T Live One.

17
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:24,075
This workflow can bring more neighbourhoods and cities into play.

18
00:01:24,075 --> 00:01:24,850
Your neighbourhood.

19
00:01:24,850 --> 00:01:25,625
Your playground.

20
00:01:25,625 --> 00:01:26,788
Blockplay S G.

21
00:01:26,788 --> 00:01:29,500
Try it at the link on screen.
